From 61ff154907bb88d2142ec2e81bb9e491b8b48271 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:51:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: cache screen metrics and the window rect until they
 change

Every read of screen.width/height/availWidth/availHeight and of
window.screenX/screenY/outerWidth/outerHeight sent a synchronous
GetScreenMetrics or GetWindowRect message to the embedder, and the reply
waits for the embedder's next event-loop spin. Pages read these in loops
and timers: 20 reads took 0.2-0.4 s (Chrome: 2000 reads in under a
millisecond), and ynet.co.il spent seconds of its first minute in them.

Window now keeps the last reply and only asks the embedder again after a
new ScriptThreadMessage::ScreenGeometryChanged. The constellation sends
it to every pipeline of a WebView when the embedder calls the new
WebView::notify_screen_geometry_changed (window moved, resized, or put on
another screen) and when the WebView's viewport is resized, so iframes
and outerWidth follow window resizes even if the embedder never calls it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
